### Image editor

I have organised my project so that in the main function I only have a loop
which reads all the commands one by one.

I have organised my files such as:

- image_editor.c: main loop
- utils.c/.h: functions that implement the commands that work with images

# MAIN function

For the implementation of this algorithm I have used a structure called `image_t`
that stores image information like format, width, height, max value of pixel
and 2 two-dimensional arrays called gray_image and color_image.

I have divided the code into 9 sections for each command:

# LOAD section

In the LOAD section, I have implemented the `load_command` function that
reads and stores information about an image in a `image_t` struct.
Before entering the `load_command` function I have freed from memory the
previously loaded images to avoid memory leaks and overwriting of the values stored.

# SELECT section

In the SELECT section, I have implemented the `select_command` function that selects
a rectangular portion of the image. Upon loading a new image,
it is automatically selected completely.

# ROTATE section

In the ROTATE section I have implemented the `rotate_command` function that rotates
the whole image or a square selection of the image by +/-90, +/-180 or +/-270 degrees.

# CROP section

In the CROP section I have implemented the `crop_command` function that reduce
the image to that contained within the current selection.

# HISTOGRAM section

In the HISTOGRAM section I have implemented the `histogram_command` function
that prints the histogram for a grayscale image.

# EQUALIZE section

In the EQUALIZE section I have implemented the `equalize_command` function that
equalizes the tones of the grayscale image by applying a mathematical equalize function.

# APPLY section

In the APPLY section I have implemented the `apply_command` function that
applies filters to color images. The 4 possible filters are EDGE, SHARPEN, BLUR
and GAUSSIAN_BLUR.

# SAVE section

In the SAVE section, I implemented the `save_command` function to save the image
in the desired data format.

# EXIT section

In the EXIT section I terminate the program by making sure I don't have any memory leaks.
